Rem Capability: clock
Rem ==================================================================
Rem clock.shoddy — Shoddy standard library: time
Rem
Rem The window-independent timing layer over the Ticks/Sleep/Clock
Rem builtins, usable by any console program — the builtins are callable
Rem without including anything; this machine is the derived layer, the
Rem way vt100.shoddy is derived from Chr.
Rem
Rem Ticks() and Clock() are deliberately different clocks. Ticks() is
Rem for MEASURING — frame pacing, deltas, benchmarks — monotonic
Rem milliseconds since program start, and the only clock animation may
Rem use. Clock() is for STAMPING — logs, filenames — a 7-element Array
Rem [year, month, day, hour, minute, second, ms] of wall-clock time,
Rem which jumps whenever the OS adjusts system time.
Rem
Rem Includes julian.shoddy for ONE word: ClockDate, the bridge from
Rem "now" to the pure calendar. Every date computation — serials,
Rem Julian day numbers, weekdays, date arithmetic — lives in julian,
Rem which never reads a clock; this machine is where a program
Rem deliberately crosses from the wall clock into that arithmetic. The
Rem direction is load-bearing: clock includes julian and never the
Rem other way round, so fin, geo and ephemeris can compute with dates
Rem while staying out of the capability system entirely.
Rem
Rem No Def here may be named Ticks, Sleep, or Clock — a Def silently
Rem shadows a builtin.
Rem ==================================================================

Rem ---- the builtins this machine is built on -------------------------
Rem
Rem NOT Defs. The engine dispatches these, and a Def whose name is a
Rem builtin is refused; they are written here because clock.shoddy is
Rem where a reader goes looking for them. The flat reference is section
Rem 10 of docs/spec.html, and the stack effects below are the ones the
Rem compiler's own Effects.cs table declares.
Rem
Rem All three are effectful — they read or yield to the world.

Rem Ticks() As Number                                 ( -- ms )
Rem     Monotonic milliseconds since the program started, fractional.
Rem     The clock for MEASURING: frame pacing, deltas, benchmarks — and
Rem     the only one animation may use, because it never jumps. Elapsed
Rem     and TimeIt below are the ordinary ways to reach it.

Rem Sleep(ms As Number)                               ( ms -- )
Rem     Yield the thread for that many milliseconds. A count of 0 or
Rem     less waits not at all. This is what a poll loop puts between
Rem     tries so a non-blocking socket or a scribbler window does not
Rem     spin a core; SleepUntil below is the deadline form.

Rem Clock() As Array Of Number                        ( -- parts )
Rem     Wall-clock now, as a 7-element ARRAY: year, month, day, hour,
Rem     minute, second, millisecond. The clock for STAMPING — logs,
Rem     filenames — and NOT for measuring: it jumps whenever the
Rem     operating system adjusts system time, which is the whole reason
Rem     Ticks exists separately. It is a flat Array rather than a record
Rem     because a builtin cannot reach a Type; Stamp and the words below
Rem     lift it into readable shapes.

Rem ---- this machine's own words --------------------------------------

Include "str.shoddy"
Include "julian.shoddy"

Rem ---- measuring -----------------------------------------------------

Def Elapsed(since As Number) As Number
    Ticks() - since

Def TimeIt(f As [ -- ]) As Number
    Let start = Ticks()
    Call(f)
    Ticks() - start

Rem Sleep whatever remains until Ticks() reaches t (nothing if past).
Def SleepUntil(t As Number)
    Sleep(Max(0, t - Ticks()))

Rem ---- stamping ------------------------------------------------------

Rem ISO-8601, e.g. "2026-07-20T14:03:07.042" — one Clock() read, so the
Rem date and time halves can never straddle midnight.
Def Stamp() As String
    Let c = Clock()
    DateOf(c) & "T" & TimeOf(c)

Def StampDate() As String
    DateOf(Clock())

Def StampTime() As String
    TimeOf(Clock())

Def DateOf(c As Array Of Number) As String
    Str(Nth(c, 1)) & "-" & PadZero(Nth(c, 2), 2) & "-" & PadZero(Nth(c, 3), 2)

Rem Today, as julian.shoddy's date record — THE ONE BRIDGE between the
Rem clock capability and the pure calendar. Everything a JulDate can do
Rem (serials, Julian day numbers, weekday, date arithmetic) stays pure
Rem in julian.shoddy; this word is where a program deliberately crosses
Rem from "now" into that arithmetic, at the edge, where the policy
Rem lives. One Clock() read, so it cannot straddle midnight.
Def ClockDate() As JulDate
    Let c = Clock()
    JulOf(Nth(c, 1), Nth(c, 2), Nth(c, 3))

Def TimeOf(c As Array Of Number) As String
    PadZero(Nth(c, 4), 2) & ":" & PadZero(Nth(c, 5), 2) & ":" & PadZero(Nth(c, 6), 2) & "." & PadZero(Nth(c, 7), 3)

Rem ---- formatting ----------------------------------------------------

Rem "1m 04.2s" for 64200; "4.2s" under a minute.
Def FormatDuration(ms As Number) As String
    Let totalSecs = ms / 1000
    Let mins = Floor(totalSecs / 60)
    Let secs = totalSecs - mins * 60
    If mins > 0 Then
        Str(mins) & "m " & PadSecs(secs) & "s"
    Else
        SecsStr(secs) & "s"

Rem Seconds to one decimal place, e.g. "4.2" ("4" when it lands whole).
Def SecsStr(s As Number) As String
    Str(Round(s * 10) / 10)

Def PadSecs(s As Number) As String
    If s < 10 Then
        "0" & SecsStr(s)
    Else
        SecsStr(s)
